Subject: dsi: use the three-bit lane swap selector on v2.4

Neo3 stock controller readback has LANE_SWAP_CTRL=0 for identity
routing. The native cold initialization writes the v2 one-hot nibble
map 0x8421, which reads back as selector 1 on both controllers.
Upstream msm DSI uses the three-bit legacy selector for this register;
reuse the existing selector helper on v2.4 while retaining the per-lane
PHY configuration and all other controller versions.

This is a display test candidate; physical output has not been verified.

--- a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_catalog.c
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_catalog.c
@@ -102,7 +102,9 @@
 	case DSI_CTRL_VERSION_2_4:
 		ctrl->ops.phy_reset_config = dsi_ctrl_hw_22_phy_reset_config;
 		ctrl->ops.config_clk_gating = dsi_ctrl_hw_22_config_clk_gating;
-		ctrl->ops.setup_lane_map = dsi_ctrl_hw_20_setup_lane_map;
+		ctrl->ops.setup_lane_map = version == DSI_CTRL_VERSION_2_4 ?
+			dsi_ctrl_hw_14_setup_lane_map :
+			dsi_ctrl_hw_20_setup_lane_map;
 		ctrl->ops.wait_for_lane_idle =
 			dsi_ctrl_hw_20_wait_for_lane_idle;
 		ctrl->ops.reg_dump_to_buffer =
